# Environment for the OpenCode server process.
#
# install.sh copies this to /etc/opencode/env, which opencode.service loads via
# EnvironmentFile=. It is the place to put credentials that must exist before a
# client ever connects, e.g. for an unattended server.
#
# After editing, restart to apply:
#   systemctl restart opencode
#
# Variable names come from the provider catalog on models.dev, or from the
# `env` list of a custom provider in opencode.jsonc. Confirmed example:
#
#   OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-...
#
# Most providers are easier to set up the other way: pair a client, run
# /connect, and enter the credential there. Credentials entered that way are
# stored on the server, not on the device you typed them into.
#
# Uncomment for verbose server activity in the log:
# OPENCODE_LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG
